WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.161
Every listing tells a story.

2
00:00:02.161 --> 00:00:03.907
The numbers tell the truth.

3
00:00:03.907 --> 00:00:12.510
In the next few minutes, I'll show you how to run a rental deal in EquityFoundry, from the listing link to a side-by-side comparison.

4
00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.680
Start at the top and pick your plan for the property:

5
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.877
a long-term rental, a short-term rental, BRRRR, or a fix and flip.

6
00:00:20.877 --> 00:00:23.166
We'll begin with a long-term rental.

7
00:00:23.966 --> 00:00:27.825
Paste the listing link from Zillow, Redfin or Realtor.com.

8
00:00:27.825 --> 00:00:34.146
EquityFoundry picks up the address and keeps the link, so the photos are always one click away.

9
00:00:34.146 --> 00:00:36.275
Give it a name you'll recognize.

10
00:00:37.075 --> 00:00:38.226
Next, the purchase.

11
00:00:38.226 --> 00:00:43.251
Enter your offer price, any repairs before you rent it out, and your closing costs.

12
00:00:43.251 --> 00:00:45.250
Not sure what a number should be?

13
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.429
Click the little i beside any field.

14
00:00:47.429 --> 00:00:51.305
It explains what it means, where to find it, and what's typical.

15
00:00:52.105 --> 00:00:53.044
Now the rent.

16
00:00:53.044 --> 00:00:55.139
Add a row for each unit type.

17
00:00:55.139 --> 00:00:58.752
This duplex has two units at twelve fifty a month.

18
00:00:58.752 --> 00:01:02.942
Vacancy starts at five percent, a sensible place to begin.

19
00:01:03.742 --> 00:01:04.599
Then the loan:

20
00:01:04.599 --> 00:01:07.475
your down payment, interest rate and loan term.

21
00:01:08.275 --> 00:01:10.704
Add the property taxes and insurance.

22
00:01:10.704 --> 00:01:18.123
Maintenance and big future repairs are already set aside as a share of the rent, so they're counted from day one.

23
00:01:18.123 --> 00:01:19.764
Using a property manager?

24
00:01:19.764 --> 00:01:21.011
Add their fee here.

25
00:01:21.811 --> 00:01:23.233
Now look to the right.

26
00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:24.525
This is your answer.

27
00:01:24.525 --> 00:01:29.049
Cash flow is what's left each month after every bill and the mortgage.

28
00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:32.539
Cash-on-cash return is what your cash earns each year.

29
00:01:32.539 --> 00:01:37.256
Cap rate weighs the property's income against its price, before any loan.

30
00:01:37.256 --> 00:01:41.004
DSCR tells a lender whether the income covers the payment.

31
00:01:41.004 --> 00:01:43.977
And the one percent rule is a quick gut check.

32
00:01:44.777 --> 00:01:51.731
The year one breakdown shows every dollar, line by line, from gross rent all the way down to cash flow.

33
00:01:52.531 --> 00:01:53.642
Numbers too tight?

34
00:01:53.642 --> 00:01:56.420
Change the price and watch everything update.

35
00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.334
That's how you find your offer.

36
00:01:59.134 --> 00:02:03.847
With Pro, the long-term projection looks thirty years down the road:

37
00:02:03.847 --> 00:02:08.352
your equity, your IRR, and what you'd walk away with at the sale.

38
00:02:08.352 --> 00:02:14.451
Pro also unlocks short-term rentals, BRRRR and flips, plus a PDF report for your lender.

39
00:02:15.251 --> 00:02:17.196
When it looks right, save it.

40
00:02:17.196 --> 00:02:20.148
The dashboard keeps every deal side by side.

41
00:02:20.148 --> 00:02:23.635
Sort by cash flow and the best one rises to the top.

42
00:02:24.435 --> 00:02:25.163
That's it.

43
00:02:25.163 --> 00:02:30.476
Run your first deal free at octopisceslabs.com/rental-calc.

44
00:02:30.476 --> 00:02:31.859
Forge better deals.
